			"widgets_values":[
				"A continuous hyper-dynamic FPV drone cinematic shot, ultra-wide 14mm lens, deep depth of field, vivid atmospheric lighting shifting across time zones, starting at dawn with cool 4000K light. T+0s-T+2s: Camera orbits the snow-capped peak of Mount Fuji at high altitude, capturing the crisp white snow against a pale morning sky with the distant Tokyo skyline silhouetted in the background. T+2s-T+4s: Camera executes a vertical nosedive, accelerating rapidly with heavy motion blur on the edges, threading through dense suburban Japanese streets, power lines, and lush green forests, creating intense spatial depth. T+4s-T+5s: A seamless hyper-lapse cloud transition pushes the camera across continents, emerging into bright 5500K midday sunlight over Paris. T+5s-T+7s: Camera hurtles toward the Eiffel Tower, threading the needle directly through the iron arches at the base, then immediately pulling up into a tight upward spiral, rotating 360 degrees around the intricate metal lattice structure. T+7s-T+8s: Camera dives off the tower apex into a thick cumulus cloud bank, emerging instantly over Rome. T+8s-T+10s: Camera flies straight through a ruined stone archway of the Colosseum, banking sharply left to whip around the massive circular interior, sunlight casting harsh geometric shadows across the ancient stone tiers, before accelerating out through the opposite side. T+10s-T+11s: Another high-speed oceanic cloud wipe transitions to New York Harbor under warm 3500K afternoon light. T+11s-T+13s: Camera approaches the Statue of Liberty, executing a sweeping upward helix maneuver around the oxidized copper statue, the Manhattan skyline shrinking into the background as altitude increases. T+13s-T+14s: Camera pushes eastward at supersonic speed, blurring mountains and clouds into streaks of color. T+14s-T+18s: Camera breaks through the clouds into a breathtaking 2500K golden hour sunset, revealing the Great Wall of China winding like a golden dragon across lush jagged peaks. Camera drops low, skimming inches above the ancient brickwork, flying straight through the narrow archway of a beacon tower, tracing the undulating ridge line, and finally pulling up into a majestic, slow-drifting ultra-wide aerial hold, the sun flaring across the lens. Environmental physics: wind violently displaces leaves in Japan (T+3s), dust kicks up inside the Colosseum (T+9s), volumetric god rays pierce through beacon tower windows (T+16s). Audio transitions: high-pitched drone rotor whine blending with roaring wind, shifting environmental acoustics from forest rustle to metallic echoes in Paris, stone reverberations in Rome, and a final sweeping orchestral crescendo mixed with mountain wind. Style: IMAX documentary, hyper-smooth stabilization, dynamic exposure ramping, zero static frames, continuous forward momentum, 60fps converted to 24fps for cinematic motion blur."
			],
